  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Lifesaving Humanitarian Assistance through Comprehensive Site Management and Coordination Services in Displacement Sites in Ma&#x2019;rib and Al Hodeidah, Yemen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To address the urgent needs of the most vulnerable populations in displacement sites across Yemen, IOM provides essential camp coordination and camp management (CCCM) activities across 53 displacement sites, hosting a total of 161,370 internally displaced persons (IDPs) or 31,207 households in Ma&apos;rib and Al Hodeidah. The intervention is strengthening IDPs&apos; access to lifesaving services and safe and dignified living conditions for people living in IDP-hosting sites and surrounding areas. IOM&apos;s CCCM field teams spearhead the coordination of IOM&apos;s multisectoral, integrated response within displacement sites, which both promotes a holistic approach to site management and reduces gaps in urgently needed services. To promote localization, IOM trains and equips community camp committees to respond to gaps in services, mitigate the impact of fires and floods, and address site care and maintenance.</narrative>
  </description>
